'' '-dll' WRITES TWO FILES, and the second one's name is the part worth pinning.
'' Measured against fbc on the same source:
''
''     -dll thing.bas                 thing.dll  AND libthing.dll.a
''     -dll thing.bas -x custom.dll   custom.dll AND libcustom.dll.a
''
'' The import library follows the OUTPUT, not the source. A test that only checked
'' the .dll would pass with the import library named after either.
''
'' THE TARGET IS NAMED IN ARGS, which overrides the one the runner puts in front of
'' every invocation -- tests/driver has no TARGETS file, so that default is win64.
'' The libraries below are windows-x86_64's, and a win64 link against them fails on
'' fbc's crt2.o rather than on anything this test is about. A later -target wins,
'' checked: 'tiko -target win64 -target windows-x86_64 --version' reports windows-x86_64.
''
'' THIS IS A REAL LINK, not a dump: a DLL needs the runtime, and on windows-x86_64 it
'' needs _DllMainCRTStartup out of lib/rt/src/c/msvccrtdll.c. TKO_LIBPATH names the
'' packaged tree because it REPLACES the bundled search rather than adding to it,
'' so the test says exactly which libraries it means.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -dll tests/codegen/src/export.bas -o tests/driver/tmpdll.dll
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0

'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/tmpdll.dll
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/libtmpdll.dll.a

'' NOT an executable. Before -dll existed the driver linked one whatever was asked.
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: tests/driver/tmpdll.exe
